      <p>You can remove a cluster that you deployed to Red Hat OpenStack Platform (RHOSP) on user-provisioned infrastructure.</p>
      <h2 id="installation-osp-downloading-modules_uninstalling-openstack-user" class="group scroll-mt-20">Downloading playbook dependencies<a href="#installation-osp-downloading-modules_uninstalling-openstack-user" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <CodeBlock code={"The Ansible playbooks that simplify the removal process on user-provisioned\ninfrastructure require several Python modules. On the machine where you will run the process,\nadd the modules' repositories and then download them."} lang="plaintext" />
      <Alert variant="note" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Note</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>These instructions assume that you are using Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) 8.</p>
        </AlertDescription>
