      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>Python 3 is installed on your machine.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      On a command line, add the following repositories:
      <ol>
      <li>
      Register with Red Hat Subscription Manager:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ sudo subscription-manager register # If not done already"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Pull the latest subscription data:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ sudo subscription-manager attach --pool=$YOUR_POOLID # If not done already"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Disable the current repositories:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ sudo subscription-manager repos --disable=* # If not done already"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Add the required repositories:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ sudo subscription-manager repos \\\n  --enable=rhel-9-for-x86_64-appstream-rpms \\\n  --enable=rhel-9-for-x86_64-baseos-rpms \\\n  --enable=openstack-17.1-for-rhel-9-x86_64-rpms"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      </li>
      <li>
      Install the modules:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ sudo yum install python3-openstackclient ansible python3-openstacksdk"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
